{"repositoryId":1345689962,"availability":"available","full":"systemslibrarian/crypto-lab-lattice-builder","name":"crypto-lab-lattice-builder","description":"Straighten a grid of dots, break a real lattice key, then watch ML-KEM run live — a playable introduction to post-quantum cryptography, with a from-scratch FIPS 203 implementation verified against all 54 of NIST's test vectors.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-25T04:50:31Z","updated":"2026-10-17T20:18:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://systemslibrarian.github.io/crypto-lab-lattice-builder/","topics":["crypto-lab","cryptography","educational","fips-203","github-pages","interactive","kyber","lattice-based-cryptography","learning-with-errors","ml-kem","post-quantum-cryptography","react","shortest-vector-problem","typescript","visualization","vite","webaudio"],"demo":"https://systemslibrarian.github.io/crypto-lab-lattice-builder/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:55.644Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:55.644Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T22:40:55.644Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-17T22:40:55.644Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Start with Beacon Run, a short navigation puzzle where changing the basis changes your jumps. The original exhibit remains available with three more ways to play: a three-field signal puzzle, Vector Flight navigation missions, and Basis Match, a six-round map-identification game. Eight dots ring HOME, the red dot at the centre of a scrambled grid. Straighten the grid with two dials until the dots light up, then take the one nearest HOME.","The exhibit is intentionally honest about its limits: it is an analogy, not an implementation or simulation of ML-KEM. Real ML-KEM uses high-dimensional module-lattice arithmetic and the hardness of learning from noisy relationships."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://git